      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Coronary artery spasm has been known to induce ischaemia and ventricular arrhythmias. We present a case of recurrent ventricular fibrillation caused by spasm-associated transmural myocardial ischaemia. During an intra-coronary acetylcholine provocation test, severe coronary spasm could be induced. The patient was treated with a hybrid approach of medication and an implantable defibrillator."},
